      ":question/id": "92ec0ae5-10b8-5071-9692-b0229385cfea",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\sqrt{3}-2\\sqrt{3}\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{5}\\right)$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Factor out $\\sqrt{3}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\sqrt{3}-2\\sqrt{3}\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{5}\\right)\\\\&\\qquad=\\sqrt{3}\\left(1-2\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{5}\\right)\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the alternative cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n1-2\\sin^2 x=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=\\frac{2\\pi}{5}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n1-2\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{5}\\right)&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{2\\pi}{5}\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(\\frac{4\\pi}{5}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the outside factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sqrt{3}\\left(1-2\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{5}\\right)\\right)&=\\sqrt{3}\\cos\\left(\\frac{4\\pi}{5}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
