      ":question/problem": "Express $4\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{15}\\right)-2$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Factor out $2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&4\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{15}\\right)-2\\\\&\\qquad=2\\left(2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{15}\\right)-1\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the alternative cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n2\\cos^2 x-1=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=\\frac{7\\pi}{15}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{15}\\right)-1&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{7\\pi}{15}\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(\\frac{14\\pi}{15}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the outside factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\left(2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{15}\\right)-1\\right)&=2\\cos\\left(\\frac{14\\pi}{15}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
